From 05dee5bf86974bb3ad76cc5b77371a6f16632671 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 06:22:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pgxp: default frame retirement OFF - it trades one artefact
 for another

Mode 1 (hard wipe) closes the gaps by suppressing correction broadly, so the
whole scene wobbles. Mode 2 (one-frame window) keeps the track looking right
but strands data the game reuses for longer than two frames - reported as the
car's wheel models wobbling. Neither is a fix.

psx_pgxp_store already resets a shadow when the guest overwrites the word with
an untracked value, so time-based retirement is redundant where the game
rewrites its vertex data each frame and actively harmful where it does not.
Left tunable for A/B; the defect to chase is the ~6% of vertices that never
receive provenance at all.
---
 runtime/src/pgxp.cpp | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/runtime/src/pgxp.cpp b/runtime/src/pgxp.cpp
index 2a4cfe8c..432cefaf 100644
--- a/runtime/src/pgxp.cpp
+++ b/runtime/src/pgxp.cpp
@@ -165,7 +165,16 @@ extern "C" int pgxp_enabled(void) { return s_enabled; }
  *     vertices fall back to rounded integer positions - wobble)
  * 2 = retire with a one-frame grace window (default): last frame's shadows
  *     stay readable, everything older is stranded. */
-static int s_frame_wipe = 2;
+/* Default 0. Both retirement modes trade one artefact for another rather than
+ * fixing either: mode 1 suppresses correction broadly (gaps close, everything
+ * wobbles), and mode 2 strands data the game reuses for more than two frames -
+ * observed as wheel models wobbling while the track looked right. Store
+ * invalidation (psx_pgxp_store) already kills a shadow when the guest
+ * overwrites the word, so time-based retirement is redundant where the game
+ * rewrites its vertex data and harmful where it does not. Kept tunable for
+ * A/B work; the real defect is the ~6% of vertices that never get provenance
+ * at all (see pgxp_resolve_state_census). */
+static int s_frame_wipe = 0;
 extern "C" void pgxp_set_frame_wipe(int mode) {
     s_frame_wipe = (mode >= 0 && mode <= 2) ? mode : 2;
 }
